Patch-Note Diff Alerts
Surface when a new patch resolves an open console bug you previously confirmed
Later

MVP (the skateboard):
Persistent chapter/collectible checklists with spoiler-guarded boss tactics.

Console-filterable bug forum with confirmation voting and verified workaround replies.

Gameplay video uploader paired with FPS / 1% Low / Frame Time telemetry and cross-console bar comparisons.

Later: User authentication/profiles, cloud object storage + transcoding for large 4K clips, and patch-note status syncing.


Not doing: Live chat rooms, automated memory-reading game overlays, ad-supported open wiki editing, or live game broadcasting.




5. 
Tech Stack
Front end
Surface: Responsive Web Application (1440px desktop sidebar workspace + mobile drawer for couch/handheld companion use).

Tools: React 19, TypeScript, Vite 8, Tailwind CSS v4, Lucide React icons, HTML5 <video> and <canvas> replay previews.

Why: Gamers already keep a browser open on a second monitor, tablet, or phone next to their console; a responsive web client requires zero installation and handles video playback and interactive checklists natively.

Back end
Piece
Choice
Why
Server / API
Node.js + Express (server.ts via tsx)
Serves REST endpoints for progress toggles, bug threads/replies, clip metadata, and Vite dev middleware from a single port 3000
Data storage
Atomic JSON store.data/waypoint-store.json  + disk video directory .data/uploads/
Zero external database setup for local/single-instance runs; supports HTTP  206 Partial Content Range streaming for smooth video  scrubbing.
Outside services (optional)
None required for MVP
Keeps local/demo runs self-contained; can swap storage later for Firestore/PostgreSQL + Cloud Storage when adding multi-user accounts.
Hosting / deploy
Single containerized Node server npm run build + npm start)
Simple deployment on Cloud Run or any Node host with persistent/object storage mounted for .data 


Architecture sketch:
Text
Browser UI (React 19 + Tailwind v4)
  ├── Overview & Interactive Guides  ──▶  POST /api/progress/toggle, /reset-chapter
  ├── Multi-Console Bug Forum        ──▶  POST /api/bugs, /:id/vote, /:id/status, /:id/replies
  └── Clips & Telemetry (<video>)    ──▶  POST /api/uploads (raw video) + POST /api/clips
                                            │
                                            ▼
                              Express Server (server.ts :3000)
                              ├── .data/waypoint-store.json (atomic state)
                              └── .data/uploads/* (HTTP Range video streaming)


